WEBVTT

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:47.650
In the middle of this century,

00:01:48.550 --> 00:01:52.550
...a single terrorist attack transformed the world.

00:01:57.060 --> 00:01:58.720
The Sheltering Sky...

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:01.470
I don't really understand it,

00:02:01.470 --> 00:02:03.560
...but they say the phenomenon comes from a magnetic abnormality.

00:02:05.940 --> 00:02:07.910
Adults say it's eerie.

00:02:08.870 --> 00:02:12.810
But for us, this is the sky we're used to seeing.

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:20.470
You were having a nightmare.

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:25.340
Well, we're here.

00:04:07.630 --> 00:04:12.650
Welcome back, my lady, Isamu, Fuko, Toru.

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:15.300
These are new guests.

00:04:15.300 --> 00:04:20.530
Kiyoko and Tatsuya Madoka, welcome to the Hotel Providence.

00:04:23.410 --> 00:04:25.540
Move it gently and carefully, please.

00:04:33.050 --> 00:04:34.520
Come this way.

00:05:05.850 --> 00:05:07.720
Tatsuya, Kiyoko...

00:05:12.620 --> 00:05:14.560
Welcome back, my lady.

00:05:15.790 --> 00:05:19.860
Welcome, Madoka family. Please fill this in.

00:05:29.940 --> 00:05:31.580
Our address...

00:05:32.510 --> 00:05:34.940
You haven't a home to return to, have you?

00:05:37.380 --> 00:05:40.650
You may write the hotel address printed there.

00:05:41.390 --> 00:05:43.850
Starting today, this is your home.

00:05:46.760 --> 00:05:49.090
What are we supposed to do?

00:05:49.760 --> 00:05:54.630
I'll think about it presently. Till then you may pass the time sleeping,

00:05:54.630 --> 00:05:58.330
...or look at the flowers in the garden. Do as you like.

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:10.150
What sort of person is she?

00:06:10.480 --> 00:06:16.390
My lady? She married into a certain noble family, but is now a widow.

00:06:17.190 --> 00:06:21.890
She inherited a vast sum, and is extremely wealthy.

00:06:24.530 --> 00:06:26.530
Has she lived in this hotel long?

00:06:26.530 --> 00:06:28.970
It must be nearly five years now.

00:06:29.430 --> 00:06:30.640
Those kids, too?

00:06:30.640 --> 00:06:33.330
Isamu and the others have been here about three years.

00:06:34.040 --> 00:06:35.970
They were scouted by my lady.

00:06:36.470 --> 00:06:38.240
Scouted?

00:06:38.240 --> 00:06:40.010
Isn't that so for you two as well?

00:06:40.650 --> 00:06:43.270
We were just bought with money.

00:06:44.350 --> 00:06:45.820
A fine joke...

00:06:47.150 --> 00:06:50.180
We have taken the liberty of preparing this room.

00:06:57.500 --> 00:06:59.520
Will this be acceptable?

00:06:59.900 --> 00:07:02.200
This? For us?

00:07:02.200 --> 00:07:05.030
Would a larger room be to your liking?

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:08.560
No, it's more than enough.

00:07:09.040 --> 00:07:10.560
What a nice garden!

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:17.780
We thank you for your patronage today.

00:07:17.780 --> 00:07:20.410
We hope you find your stay most relaxing.

00:07:27.530 --> 00:07:29.390
Oh, this is comfy!

00:07:30.960 --> 00:07:33.060
Here, over here, Toru.

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:34.460
Wait!

00:07:37.200 --> 00:07:39.640
Hey, hey! Come over here!

00:07:40.310 --> 00:07:42.430
I can't find you!

00:07:42.710 --> 00:07:44.700
Use your Dynamis!

00:07:45.340 --> 00:07:47.110
Come over here!

00:07:47.110 --> 00:07:49.210
You're making fun of me!

00:07:49.210 --> 00:07:50.680
What is it?

00:07:52.550 --> 00:07:54.040
This is so strange, somehow.

00:07:55.420 --> 00:07:57.460
At this time just yesterday,

00:07:57.460 --> 00:08:00.320
...we were hiding from the rain under a piano.

00:08:05.200 --> 00:08:07.100
So you ended up bringing it.

00:08:08.300 --> 00:08:10.600
I hadn't intended to.

00:08:13.540 --> 00:08:19.140
That woman was saying our power is needed for fighting Gilgamesh.

00:08:19.840 --> 00:08:23.410
Even though we don't have amazing power like those kids.

00:08:24.350 --> 00:08:25.910
Do we?

00:08:26.420 --> 00:08:27.710
No way...

00:08:32.160 --> 00:08:36.350
The Countess, Orga, and Gilgamesh...

00:08:43.900 --> 00:08:46.430
I wonder what Gilgamesh is?

00:08:46.840 --> 00:08:48.810
Gi... Gi...

00:08:51.280 --> 00:08:52.240
It's there?

00:08:52.240 --> 00:08:57.210
In an age when humans were gods, assailed by a great Deluge, a city fell.

00:08:57.750 --> 00:09:00.490
That's Noah's Ark, isn't it?

00:09:00.490 --> 00:09:02.490
Says it's "The Epic of Gilgamesh."

00:09:02.490 --> 00:09:04.680
So the Bible wasn't first.

00:09:05.690 --> 00:09:11.730
Gilgamesh was a king, part man, part god, descended from survivors of this Deluge.

00:09:11.730 --> 00:09:16.220
With his great friend Enkidu, he set off on a journey of adventure.

00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:23.460
He killed a monster who ruled a forest and founded Uruk, the world's first city.

00:09:24.210 --> 00:09:30.280
The capricious goddess Ishtar fell in love with Gilgamesh and desired him for her husband,

00:09:30.280 --> 00:09:34.720
...but Gilgamesh, knowing her true nature, refused.

00:09:34.720 --> 00:09:42.490
Mad with rage, Ishtar demanded the gods send the Bull of Heaven to Uruk, to destroy it.

00:09:42.490 --> 00:09:47.060
But Gilgamesh, combining his might with Enkidu's, slew the Bull.

00:09:48.500 --> 00:09:52.840
For this, the gods set Enkidu's death as the penalty,

00:09:52.840 --> 00:09:56.170
...and he fell ill and departed this world.

00:09:57.910 --> 00:09:59.880
Gilgamesh, grief-stricken,

00:09:59.880 --> 00:10:03.870
...set out on an endless journey in search of eternal life.

00:10:10.790 --> 00:10:13.850
So Enkidu came from this.

00:10:14.490 --> 00:10:18.960
I always assumed it was just the Chinese pronunciation of Dad's name.

00:10:20.700 --> 00:10:23.740
Madoka Terumichi... En-ki-dou...

00:10:37.920 --> 00:10:39.380
My lady, look at this.

00:10:57.070 --> 00:10:59.760
We've been bathed in direct gamma radiation.

00:11:05.310 --> 00:11:12.340
Antimatter... So Gilgamesh are not made of the substance of this world.

00:11:12.750 --> 00:11:14.420
What do you mean, my lady?

00:11:14.420 --> 00:11:17.460
They're made of a substance from another universe.

00:11:17.460 --> 00:11:21.320
But if it's antimatter, it can't exist in this world...

00:11:22.060 --> 00:11:24.120
Observe...

00:11:24.660 --> 00:11:26.530
Atoms of antimatter,

00:11:26.530 --> 00:11:30.160
...each coated by molecules of our world's matter.

00:11:30.940 --> 00:11:34.460
Gilgamesh are fearsome indeed.

00:11:36.840 --> 00:11:41.440
To cleanly sever part of a body that ought to be unbreakable...

00:11:42.010 --> 00:11:46.110
Perhaps the truly fearsome one is he who used that power.

00:11:48.220 --> 00:11:51.880
But in any case, there is too much that we don't yet understand.

00:11:52.960 --> 00:11:58.330
If we could capture one alive just once... That's a task to pursue.

00:12:35.330 --> 00:12:38.000
Would you care to play?

00:12:40.270 --> 00:12:41.940
Would it be okay?

00:12:41.940 --> 00:12:43.240
Please...

00:12:44.280 --> 00:12:45.570
Thanks...

00:14:30.680 --> 00:14:32.380
Wow! You're good!

00:14:33.520 --> 00:14:35.610
I haven't been playing much.

00:14:41.030 --> 00:14:42.460
It's dinner time.

00:14:42.460 --> 00:14:43.930
Let's go.

00:14:57.040 --> 00:14:59.570
Hey, next time teach me to play too!

00:15:00.910 --> 00:15:01.880
Okay.

00:15:02.610 --> 00:15:04.010
I mean it.

00:15:06.820 --> 00:15:09.450
That's amazing. How did you learn to...

00:15:09.790 --> 00:15:12.120
Just somehow.

00:15:12.790 --> 00:15:14.190
Same as anything.

00:15:14.190 --> 00:15:16.160
Like the first time you manage to do a pullover in gymnastics...

00:15:16.160 --> 00:15:17.790
...or when you first learn to ride a bike.

00:15:19.600 --> 00:15:22.330
So someday you'll get it too.

00:15:22.530 --> 00:15:24.160
I doubt it.

00:15:29.210 --> 00:15:31.210
Kept you waiting!

00:15:31.210 --> 00:15:33.880
Well? You're comfortable here?

00:15:33.880 --> 00:15:35.370
Yes...

00:15:39.220 --> 00:15:40.450
What do you recommend?

00:15:40.450 --> 00:15:44.320
This evening, might I recommend the Chateaubriand with an ice wine?

00:15:51.160 --> 00:15:54.190
Was that you playing the piano just now, Kiyoko?

00:15:55.070 --> 00:15:56.000
Yes...

00:15:56.000 --> 00:15:58.400
I said you may do as you like,

00:15:58.400 --> 00:16:01.800
...but will you refrain from poor piano playing?

00:16:05.480 --> 00:16:08.310
Especially, before meals.

00:16:11.480 --> 00:16:13.040
One moment, please.

00:16:22.230 --> 00:16:23.820
My lady, the wing has...

00:16:30.270 --> 00:16:32.740
So much for our nice dinner.

00:16:33.500 --> 00:16:35.840
Well, let's go.

00:16:35.840 --> 00:16:39.210
You two need to get used to carnage as well.

00:16:39.710 --> 00:16:43.080
Even if we go, we'll just be a hindrance.

00:16:43.080 --> 00:16:44.150
You're afraid?

00:16:44.150 --> 00:16:46.080
That's not why I said it!

00:16:46.580 --> 00:16:48.450
Then let's go.

00:16:55.490 --> 00:16:56.460
My lady!

00:16:56.460 --> 00:16:57.800
The other guests?

00:16:57.800 --> 00:16:59.530
Evacuation is complete.

00:16:59.530 --> 00:17:01.660
Sorry for the inconvenience.

00:17:02.070 --> 00:17:06.400
Oh, no, it's another form of our Hotel Providence service.

00:17:06.870 --> 00:17:09.000
Your saying so is a great help.

00:17:09.370 --> 00:17:11.040
You too now, quickly.

00:17:11.040 --> 00:17:12.770
I shall take advantage of my lady's kindness.

00:17:32.500 --> 00:17:33.960
So fast!

00:17:51.450 --> 00:17:52.920
Going below, is it?

00:18:14.240 --> 00:18:15.710
Oh, no!

00:18:44.000 --> 00:18:45.470
Tatsuya...

00:19:25.010 --> 00:19:31.040
That's why I said we need you two to fight Gilgamesh.

00:19:39.920 --> 00:19:43.490
The piano's ruined.

00:20:32.310 --> 00:20:33.780
What's wrong?

00:20:38.280 --> 00:20:42.240
Kiyoko, is something happening with my body?

00:20:42.920 --> 00:20:44.190
Something?

00:20:44.190 --> 00:20:46.050
How could something like that...

00:20:48.390 --> 00:20:51.860
There's nothing wrong. You're the same Tatsuya as always.

00:20:51.860 --> 00:20:54.350
That stuff has to be some kind of trick.

00:20:55.070 --> 00:20:57.200
Could it be Dad's...

00:20:57.200 --> 00:21:01.810
It's nothing to do with Dad. I know you better than anyone.

00:21:01.810 --> 00:21:04.330
If I'm saying it, it must be right.

00:21:04.680 --> 00:21:06.140
Right.

00:21:07.040 --> 00:21:09.050
It looks like you've grown again.

00:21:09.050 --> 00:21:11.020
I'm already taller than you.

00:21:11.020 --> 00:21:12.480
No, you're not!

00:21:24.430 --> 00:21:26.420
Say, Tatsuya...

00:21:28.500 --> 00:21:33.030
Shall we run away after all? From here?

00:23:24.950 --> 00:23:27.580
Though they're brother and sister, they're different.

00:23:27.580 --> 00:23:29.020
It's plain as day.

00:23:29.020 --> 00:23:30.750
What a fine big brother!

00:23:30.750 --> 00:23:35.190
Just don't play that piece, that concerto from before.

00:23:35.190 --> 00:23:37.690
You two, go back to your rooms immediately.

00:23:37.690 --> 00:23:40.230
You can sleep with me tonight.

00:23:40.230 --> 00:23:43.730
It's nothing to fear, just because you're different from other people.

00:23:43.730 --> 00:23:45.600
Yes, special.

00:23:45.600 --> 00:23:47.760
Now it should be a little easier on you.

00:23:48.110 --> 00:23:50.200
Just as I thought, Tatsuya.

00:23:50.840 --> 00:23:53.210
You have amazing power locked inside you.
